  "fanTake": "Well, that's what a defensive showcase looks like, even if our offense couldn't quite get into rhythm. Twenty to three at home against Pittsburgh — we held them to a field goal and forced them into a third-down conversion rate of 17%, which is the kind of defensive suffocation that makes you forget about our own anemic 33% on third down and mediocre red-zone execution (1 of 3 touchdowns when we should be hitting closer to 55%). Romeo Doubs was absolutely magnificent, turning in a +14% win probability added performance and keeping us in business when everything else felt a bit clunky. Our offense posted a negative EPA per play, which stings on principle, but our defense's -0.36 EPA allowed was genuinely exceptional — that's the real story here. Sometimes you win ugly, and sometimes ugly looks pretty good when you're talking about Gillette Stadium on a September afternoon.",
